   |  P·R·O·G·R·A·M   D·E·S·C·R·I·P·T·I·O·N
_ _¦__________________________________________________ __ _
   :

    noC-SDOPP, (Senseless Destruction of Public Property), is a simple wall
    door  with  a  great  looking  display.    Possibly one of the simplest
    products  of nocTurne deSign to date, it is still well-tested and looks
    cool.                                                                    :
                                                                             ¦
                                                                             |
_ _:_________________________________________________________________________|__
   ¦                                                                         ¦
   |  I·N·S·T·A·L·L·A·T·I·O·N                                                :
_ _¦__________________________________________________ __ _
   :

    This program requires OS2.0 or greater.

    Simply  copy the 'noC-SDOPP' drawer into 'DOORS:' and mount the door as
    is  convention  with  your particular version of Ami/Sigma Express.  (A
    BBSCMD icon is provided for 3.xx users).

    Most sysops choose to install walls as a part of their login procedure.
    noC-SDOPP may be run from an MCI command, or from the main menu.  It is  ·
    up to you how to use it.                                                 :
                                                                             ¦
_ _:_________________________________________________________________________|__
   ¦                                                                         ¦
   |  P·R·O·G·R·A·M   L·O·G·I·C                                              :
_ _¦__________________________________________________ __ _
   :

    Usage  is  very  intuitive.   The user, after being shown an attractive
    wall decorated with phrases of grandeur, may choose to enter his own 76
    character  contribution.    All  text  data   is   kept   in   the file
    "DOORS:noC-SDOPP/noC-SDOPP.data".   To clear the wall, this file should  .
    be deleted.                                                              :
                                                                             ¦
